{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 11, :comments ["<b>And it shall be when YHWH brings you to the land of the Canaanite</b> — because the commandment of פטר חמור (the firstling of a donkey) applies only in the Land. And according to the plain sense of 'Sanctify to Me every firstborn' — all those found among Israel that day, for since He redeemed them from death when He struck the land of Egypt, He commanded that they be holy to Him, to perform the service of YHWH in all that He would command concerning them. And He did not command them redemption at that time, until He exchanged them for the Levites and commanded the redemption of the excess (Numbers 3:46). But the commandment concerning those born afterward did not apply in the wilderness; rather, He commanded that when they come into the Land, it shall apply to man and beast and to פטר חמור, and He commanded their redemption for all generations." "And the sense of <b>as He swore to you and to your fathers</b> is that He swore to your fathers to give it to you, as He said above (Exodus 13:5): 'which He swore to your fathers to give you.' Or else the word of HaShem may be called an oath, for He said so twice: 'and I have come down to deliver him and to bring him up from that land to a good and spacious land' (Exodus 3:8), and further: 'and I will bring you to the land concerning which I lifted My hand' (Exodus 6:8)."], :book :exodus, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 13, :notes {0 "The word העודפים ('the excess') refers to the firstborn Israelites who outnumbered the Levites, as described in Numbers 3:46–51."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T04:16:47.360817223Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}